WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:05.639
Catwoman is a familiar face – but you've
never seen her, or Zoe Kravitz, quite like

00:00:05.639 --> 00:00:06.639
this.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:10.910
"The Batman" gives audiences a brand-new version
of Gotham City where the Dark Knight has already

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:16.019
been operating for two years when the Riddler
rears his head to root out the corrupt officials

00:00:16.019 --> 00:00:18.609
who take advantage of the power they have.

00:00:18.609 --> 00:00:22.380
The film also sees Bruce Wayne struggling
with his parents' legacy when the Riddler's

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.390
mission involves secrets from his family's
past.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:29.470
It seems like this new take on the Caped Crusader
will take a different approach to the classic

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.779
story than the one fans are familiar with.

00:00:31.779 --> 00:00:34.989
Pattinson recently opened up about the role
to GQ, explaining,

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:40.239
"He doesn't have a playboy persona at all,
so he's kind of a weirdo as Bruce and a weirdo

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:44.179
as Batman, and I kept thinking there's a more
nihilistic slant to it."

00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:48.449
Thankfully, this weirdo has a few allies on
his side to keep him on the straight and narrow

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:50.679
when taking on the criminals of Gotham.

00:00:50.679 --> 00:00:56.089
One of those allies is more of a frenemy – a
mysterious cat burglar who has ties to the

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.089
mob.

00:00:57.089 --> 00:01:02.379
Her name is Selina Kyle, aka Catwoman, and
she's brought to life this time by Zoe Kravitz.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:07.590
Back in 2011, Zoë Kravitz joined the dramedy
series "Californication," which stars David

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:11.810
Duchovny as Hank Moody — a writer with a
penchant for drinking, drugs, and numerous

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:15.020
affairs — while trying to keep his daughter,
Becca, happy.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:19.480
Kravitz shows up in Season 4 as Pearl, the
singer of an all-girl rock band called Queens

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:22.400
of Dogtown — and she invites Becca to join
the group.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.500
Pearl and Becca get up to plenty of mischief
over the course of the series, even stealing

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.430
Hank's Porsche in one episode.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:32.360
Kravitz's performance as Pearl shows she can
have a lot of fun with a role, although the

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.180
writers couldn't resist making a joke about
her famous father, Lenny Kravitz.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.520
In the series, Pearl's dad, Ben, is dating
Hank's ex-girlfriend, Karen Van Der Beek — and

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:45.600
the troubled writer has a meta joke about
Ben, referring to him, derisively, as "Lenny

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.600
Kravitz."

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.310
"Speaking of dark, how's Lenny Kravitz?"

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.310
"Excuse me?"

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:53.700
"The Batman" may be Zoe Kravitz' biggest movie
yet, but it's not her first outing in the

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.060
superhero genre.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:59.740
Her first comic book role came in 2011 when
she starred in "X-Men: First Class," Fox's

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.590
first mutant prequel.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:05.930
Zoë Kravitz plays Angel Salvadore — also
known as Tempest in the comics — a mutant

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.940
with insect wings and the ability to spit
acid.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.450
She starts out with the good guys, but things
don't stay that way, and she ends up fighting

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.390
her former friends in the movie's dramatic
ending.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:19.090
It's a surprising move from Angel, who initially
seems quite happy with their mission to help

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.160
mutants.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.130
But Kravitz's work in the role proves that
she can hold her own against other huge stars

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:26.200
in a big-budget comic book movie.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:30.690
The star masterfully navigates Angel's moral
ambiguity, which is definitely useful when

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:33.090
it comes to playing Catwoman in "The Batman."

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.910
Zoë Kravitz once again proved that she can
work well in a big franchise when she joined

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:41.500
the Wizarding World, prominently appearing
in the second film in the "Fantastic Beasts"

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:46.240
series, "Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald,"
as Leta Lestrange.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.900
Unfortunately, it doesn't seem like Leta will
return in future "Fantastic Beasts" films

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:56.010
since she sacrifices herself to save her fiance,
Theseus, and her old friend Newt from the

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.470
Dark wizard Gellert Grindelwald.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:02.670
Then again, this is a franchise all about
magic, so it's not impossible she could return

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:03.670
somehow.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:08.150
Zoë Kravitz also recently showed off the
true extent of her talent in HBO's buzzy drama

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:12.880
"Big Little Lies," playing Bonnie Carlson
opposite the likes of Reese Witherspoon, Nicole

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.709
Kidman, Shailene Woodley, and Laura Dern.

00:03:15.709 --> 00:03:19.570
In the first season, Bonnie is in the background
of the show; she is quite happy in her marriage

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:22.430
with Nathan and gets on well with his daughter
Abigail.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:26.930
Unfortunately, as more secrets reveal themselves
about the Monterey residents, Bonnie's life

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.880
is turned upside down.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.630
Kravitz's performance really excels after
Season 1's shocking finale, which forces the

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:36.990
Monterey Five to hide more secrets from the
authorities to make sure none of them end

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.130
up going to prison.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.820
Without getting into spoilers, the weight
of Bonnie's turmoil causes her to push her

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.770
husband away, and she even lashes out at her
mother when she comes to Monterey to help

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:46.770
her.

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:50.150
Kravitz really shows her range in "Big Little
Lies," and according to the critics, she brings

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:54.180
that same complexity to Selina Kyle in "The
Batman."

